---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  fullTitle="About Us | Best Shanghai Restaurants Guide"
  description="Learn how Best Shanghai Restaurants helps travelers discover authentic Shanghai cuisine, from xiaolongbao to red-braised pork, in China and abroad."
>
  <main>
    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-20 md:pt-28 pb-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl tracking-tighter leading-none font-semibold text-slate-900">About Us</h1>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10">Our Story</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-6 text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
          <p>Best Shanghai Restaurants was born from a simple frustration: finding truly great Shanghai cuisine outside of China is hard. The internet is full of outdated lists, paid placements, and reviews from people who have never tasted real xiaolongbao.</p>
          <p>We are a team of food writers, chefs, and obsessive eaters who have spent years exploring Shanghai's dining scene. From the narrow lanes of the Old City to the glimmering towers of Lujiazui, we have eaten our way through thousands of meals to bring you honest, informed recommendations.</p>
          <p>Our mission is simple: help you discover the best Shanghai restaurants wherever you are. Whether you are in Shanghai itself or searching for authentic Shanghainese food in New York, London, or Sydney, our guides are built on real experience and a deep love for this extraordinary cuisine.</p>
          <p>We dine anonymously, pay for our own meals, and revisit restaurants regularly. No free meals, no sponsored placements, no compromises.</p>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10">Our Commitment</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-500 mt-4">Every recommendation is backed by first-hand experience. No shortcuts, no compromises.</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-slate-500 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>We pay our own way.</strong> No comped meals, no press trips, no gifted tasting menus. If we did not buy the dish, we do not review it.</li>
          <li><strong>We eat anonymously.</strong> Reservations are made under ordinary names so that how we are treated reflects how you will be treated.</li>
          <li><strong>We revisit.</strong> A single great visit is not enough. Restaurants stay on the list only while they hold their standard across multiple visits, in different seasons, at different times of day.</li>
          <li><strong>We update, and we admit when things change.</strong> Kitchens change chefs, prices drift, service slips. Dates on every guide show when a page was last checked against reality.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10">What Sets This Guide Apart</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-6 text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
          <p>Most English-language coverage of Shanghai dining was written for a different audience or a different decade. It leans on hotel concierge recommendations, recycles the same five tourist-address names, or treats "Chinese food" as a single undifferentiated category. Shanghai cuisine is none of those things. Benbang home cooking, the soup dumplings of the Old City, the autumn hairy-crab ritual, and the world-class fine-dining scene that has grown up along the Bund are distinct traditions, and they reward being explained properly.</p>
          <p>So we write for the traveler who wants to eat like a local without speaking the language. That means practical detail over adjectives: how to order, what to say, how to pay, when to arrive to skip the queue, and what a fair price actually looks like. Every restaurant page is built to answer the questions you would ask a well-read friend who happens to live in Shanghai — because that, in the end, is exactly what we are trying to be.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6">
          <a href="/" class="btn-soft bg-accent-600 hover:bg-accent-700 text-white text-sm font-medium px-6 py-3 transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-2">Explore Our Top Picks</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
